WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.827
A materialized view is different from a standard view because it stores the query result.

00:00:05.827 --> 00:00:08.772
Think of it as a prepared snapshot.

00:00:08.772 --> 00:00:14.042
Suppose a dashboard needs the same expensive summary again and again.

00:00:14.042 --> 00:00:20.727
Instead of recalculating the summary every time, we can store the result in a materialized view.

00:00:21.415 --> 00:00:23.937
That can make repeated reads faster.

00:00:23.937 --> 00:00:29.367
But now we have a new responsibility: the stored snapshot can become old.

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:35.516
So whenever you use a materialized view, you must think about both performance and freshness.
